1.5 Method

This is a theoretical dissertation. It produces:

1. A formal model of verification under sovereignty, with explicit epistemic status for each component.
2. A set of propositions with proofs about the limits of each regime.
3. A regime formation game with a richer participation space and an equilibrium selection analysis.
4. A pre-registered experimental design using the ADEMP framework.
5. A specification of falsification criteria.
6. A taxonomy of failure modes.
7. An honest inventory of what the theory does not establish.

1.6 What this dissertation is not

It is not a manifesto. It does not claim that conflict can be eliminated. It does not assume that states will trust each other. It does not claim that any technical mechanism can substitute for political will. It does not contain empirical validation of any kind. It does not claim that the verification paradox is resolved—only that it is a research program.

