Appendix E. Simulation Design Specification

This appendix specifies the design of the ADEMP simulation. No simulation has been executed. No code has been trained. No physical tests have been performed. This is a pre-registered design awaiting execution.

E.1 Aims

The simulation aims to estimate the effect of distributed, contestable verification on detection delay, subject to non-inferiority constraints on false positives, cost, participation, and rights. The primary hypothesis is

H_1: \quad \Delta_{21}^{\text{RMST}} = \frac{\text{RMST}_1(H) - \text{RMST}_2(H)}{\text{RMST}_1(H)} \geq 0.20,

with secondary hypothesis

H_2: \quad \text{WMST}_2(H, \tau_0) \geq \text{WMST}_1(H, \tau_0) \quad \text{for } \tau_0 > 0.

E.2 Data-Generating Mechanisms

The simulation is structured as a Monte Carlo replication study. Each replication samples parameters from the grid in Table E.1 and simulates the verification process over a time horizon $H$.

