Appendix F. Falsification Protocol

F.1 Primary Falsification Criteria

Criterion F.1 (Detection efficacy). If $\Delta_{21}^{\text{RMST}} < 0.20$, $H_1$ is not supported.

Criterion F.2 (False positives). If the non-inferiority margin is exceeded vs $R_1$, the regime fails.

Criterion F.3 (Cost). If administrative cost + independence-audit cost $> 15\%$ of total agreement cost, the regime fails.

Criterion F.4 (Participation). If participation drops $> 25\%$ vs $R_0$, the regime fails.

Criterion F.5 (Manipulation). If vulnerability exceeds the pre-registered margin under coordinated attack, the regime fails.

Criterion F.6 (Rights). Any violation of a mandatory constraint is a design failure.

Criterion F.7 (Humanitarian suspension). If simulation shows aid suspended during $Q_t = U$, the design fails.

Criterion F.8 (Graceful degradation). Under majority capture, status must transition to $I$.

Criterion F.9 (Equilibrium selection). If no exogenous catalyst is present, the regime must not be claimed self-sustaining.

Criterion F.10 (Legitimacy contestation). If legitimacy contestation indefinitely blocks findings, the design fails.

Criterion F.11 (Discrete capture). If Poisson capture events cause $\hat{\rho} > \rho_{\max}$ without triggering fail-safe, the design fails.

Criterion F.12 (Sensor authentication). If sources without authentication produce non-inferior detection, the maturity model is not empirically necessary.

Criterion F.13 (Situation-structure mismatch). If $R_2$ outperforms $R_1$ in a CO domain, or $R_1$ outperforms $R_2$ in an AS domain, Proposition 3.2 is falsified.

Criterion F.14 (Capture-game equilibrium). If observed protection levels deviate from $q_e^*$ by more than a pre-registered margin, the capture game is misspecified.

Criterion F.15 (Normative contagion). If $\Lambda$ does not depreciate under great-power exemption, the normative contagion model is falsified.

Criterion F.16 (Reciprocity pathway). If great-power verification levels do not increase under the reciprocity pathway, the pathway is not credible.

Criterion F.17 (WMST vs RMST). If WMST does not achieve higher power than RMST when curves cross, Proposition 6.2 is falsified.

F.2 Secondary Falsification Criteria

Criterion F.18 (Novel formalizations). If any novel formalization is tested and fails, it must be revised or deleted.

Criterion F.19 (Caveated applications). If the design choices in caveated applications are shown to be empirically unjustified, the applications must be revised.

Criterion F.20 (Source reliability). If any validated source is retracted or contradicted, the propositions depending on it must be re-evaluated.

